WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.100
- All right, y'all it's
time for my first guest.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.155
She is a perfect example of
why you should never give up.

00:00:05.155 --> 00:00:06.860
She's persevered through almost

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.427
a decade of rejection
in Hollywood and music,

00:00:09.427 --> 00:00:10.790
now she's starring in

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:14.180
one of the biggest
shows on TV, This is Us.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.940
And last year, a song she sang
was nominated for an Oscar.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.930
This year, she releases her
first album of country music

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.070
and I cannot wait to hear it, I love her.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.080
Let's all say hi to Chrissy Metz.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.260
What's up Chrissy, how you doing?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.740
- Good, how are you?

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.560
- I am so good. It's lovely to see you,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.730
by the way you look beautiful,

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.093
I love you in a ponytail.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.540
- Listen, thank you. I
got about two hairstyles.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.634
It's up and sometimes straightened down.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:41.520
(laughter)

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.620
- Here's mine, this is
mine when it doesn't work,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.740
like I curled my hair this morning

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.190
and it just was like, what
the hell is happening?

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.650
So I just pin it back.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.941
That's when I just pin it back a bit,

00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:50.893
- You go.

00:00:50.893 --> 00:00:51.770
- And I'm like, I went for this,

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.930
I didn't, I hate being here in makeup.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.480
- Nobody would have known, not one person.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.313
- Well, you're kind,

00:00:58.313 --> 00:00:59.157
I understand you've been holding it down

00:00:59.157 --> 00:01:02.120
in one of my favorite
cities, are you in Nashville?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.603
- I am since the beginning of March, Yeah.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.690
- Were you there like working

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.100
and then were just kind of were
like, okay, I'm stuck here.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.345
- No, we came out to finish
the back half of my album.

00:01:12.345 --> 00:01:13.612
- That's what I meant.

00:01:13.612 --> 00:01:16.440
- Yeah. And then the record
just stopped literally.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.943
And so, yeah, we've been here Donnie and I

00:01:18.943 --> 00:01:21.430
have just been stuck, thank
goodness I have him here,

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.740
but we've been stuck.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.584
- Oh my gosh. Right? Yeah, I wouldn't,

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.360
I know I have friends that
I sometimes get jealous of

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.064
when they're like at home
alone without children,

00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:30.330
but for the most part,

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.540
I think for months that would have,

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.190
I would have gone insane.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.223
I have to be around at least one human.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.360
- Right!

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.610
- So, so it is you and your
best friend, Donnie, right?

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.578
That y'all been, y'all been
finding ways to stay busy.

00:01:42.578 --> 00:01:43.530
- We've been trying.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.750
- I need you to tell us about
these tetherball battles

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.730
and how much I love that
you're playing tetherball

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.610
'cause that's like my childhood.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.640
- Right? Third grade I literally was like,

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.446
what can we do in the
confines of a backyard?

00:01:55.446 --> 00:01:58.360
I got a regulation tetherball
folks is what I did

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.373
from the Internets.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.460
I was like, Donnie, let's play,

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.500
well, he's not very versed on tetherball.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.920
I am, however, and I'm
also super competitive,

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.268
which is obnoxious.

00:02:08.268 --> 00:02:09.101
- Me too.

00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:10.363
- Let's just say I had.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:13.920
This pinky won't go all the way down.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.390
I have jammed this pinky and I can't,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.360
I don't know what's happened guys.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.060
So, Donnie starts kicking the ball

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.368
and I'm starting to like, you know,

00:02:23.368 --> 00:02:25.887
it got competitive and
got a little heated.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.520
- I was the same way, but you know,

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.470
every kid that grew up,

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:31.270
not in like the richest neighborhood,

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.883
if you know what tetherball is.

00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:33.936
(laughter)

00:02:33.936 --> 00:02:35.067
- Right. Right.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.500
- Cause that was like a

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.470
cheap thing to have on the
playground for all of us.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.700
So I love tetherball,
I think it's amazing.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.220
Well, congratulations on your
recent music deal, by the way.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.757
That's really cool.

00:02:46.757 --> 00:02:49.150
The first song you released
is called 'Talking to God'.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.590
So what's that about?

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.832
- So that was found on Ashley
McBride writer's retreat.

00:02:53.832 --> 00:02:55.056
- Oh he's great!

00:02:55.056 --> 00:02:58.880
- And I knew, I knew all the
writers on the retreat and I,

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.340
my manager was like, Oh, you know,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.760
they wrote the song
this week and I'm like,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.520
I want to hear it, and I
just fell in love with it.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.944
It was one of those songs
where I didn't write,

00:03:06.944 --> 00:03:09.990
I didn't have any, any sort of, you know,

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.810
time spent on the song, but I just was.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:13.670
- Connected.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.599
- Yeah, it just, it
felt so important to me.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:18.650
And I get it that like, you
know, we all make decisions

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.597
or wish we would have
made different decisions,

00:03:20.597 --> 00:03:22.060
and we all think about people

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.580
who aren't in our lives anymore.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.030
And you know, it just resonated with me.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.970
So I was like, I want to cut it.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:28.823
Could I please.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.100
- And I mean,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.870
we've touched on this a
little in the past with you,

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:34.730
but isn't it true

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.350
that you didn't want to sing as a child?

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.250
Like you wanted to be in a band?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.960
- Well, no, no. I wanted to sing,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.650
that's what I wanted to do.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.880
I really wanted to sing,

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.830
but I was too afraid of my own shadow.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:48.470
And because my mom couldn't
afford an instrument

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.480
and all the cool kids were in band.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.660
I was, Oh, I guess I'll join
choir because it's free.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.781
- Girl, that's me.

00:03:56.781 --> 00:03:57.614
(laughter)

00:03:57.614 --> 00:04:00.550
- Right. I'm like, okay.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:04.160
Right, and so it felt really
comfortable to be one of many,

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.420
but still like, understand
like the blending

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.650
and the technique and all that stuff.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.190
And that was really
super fun and important

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.270
and that's really where I got, I mean,

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.060
I've always had a love for
music cause I grew up with it,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.097
but actually doing it,

00:04:16.097 --> 00:04:20.280
and the safety of a
choir was the beginning.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.560
- Yeah, and I always love like growing up

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.830
in a choir as well, in that surrounding,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.120
and I was too poor to play.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.120
I couldn't be in band either,

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.990
cause we didn't have
money, and this was free.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.310
So I get you. I feel you there,

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.120
honestly, being in that
choir, being in those,

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.670
around those personalities
of kids that were,

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.090
we were all just oddballs.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.190
Like we were very nerdy.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.090
Like, you know, none of
us were cool and we just,

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.690
we're just figuring out
our own personalities.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:41.620
I think that really helps.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.430
So I, I love that you,

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.910
you love to sing and you were like, well,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.724
I just didn't want to
be in the spotlight yet.

00:04:47.724 --> 00:04:50.160
So knowing that is amazing
too about yourself.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.580
So Chrissy, the five most
recent episodes of This Is Us

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.440
start streaming on Peacock
TV today, which is awesome

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.540
'cause all these streaming services

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.780
are really bringing new life to shows.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.220
So are y'all excited about that?

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.117
- Yeah, absolutely. I think, you know,

00:05:02.117 --> 00:05:04.660
a lot of people don't
necessarily have the time

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.870
or didn't have the time
and now they have the time

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.181
or have the ability to even access it.

00:05:09.181 --> 00:05:11.880
You're right though,
there is so many people

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.170
in this world that haven't seen it,

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.420
even though it's an international show

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.253
- Exactly!

00:05:16.253 --> 00:05:17.830
- And if you can make things
convenient for people,

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.190
I think they're more inclined to watch it

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.670
and then they're like hooked.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.058
Cause it's just such a real raw, you know.

00:05:23.058 --> 00:05:24.400
- I just find it interesting.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.440
I'm excited about the peacock thing

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.350
because this brings new
life to all these show

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.560
that like could make a
really big impact on people

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:31.870
that just didn't know
they were even ever going

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.223
to get to see it.

00:05:33.223 --> 00:05:34.105
- Right.

00:05:34.105 --> 00:05:35.570
- So, so how, how have you been keeping up

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:36.842
speaking of This Is Us, do y'all have,

00:05:36.842 --> 00:05:38.590
I know that you get in these casts,

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.430
especially these really success ones,

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.500
y'all are on there for seasons,

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.300
like have you all been
able to catch up at all?

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.550
Have y'all zoomed at all or done anything.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.859
- Yes, we have done the
zoom, we have zoom zammed.

00:05:47.859 --> 00:05:49.959
And it was so sweet because Justin Hartley

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.248
who plays Kevin, he's the one that's like,

00:05:54.248 --> 00:05:56.954
Hey guys, do you want
to Zoom? And we're like,

00:05:56.954 --> 00:05:58.323
(laughter)

00:05:58.323 --> 00:05:59.156
- I love that.

00:05:59.156 --> 00:05:59.989
- And that's just Justin,

00:05:59.989 --> 00:06:01.840
he's not just a handsome
guy who's super talented,

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.370
he has the biggest heart.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.710
And so it was so cute that he was the one

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:05.740
that wanted to arrange it.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.740
So, and then Chris arranged, you know,

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.227
the actual appointment
time and called it the

00:06:10.227 --> 00:06:14.694
"Miguel Rivas Fan Club", which
Jon Huertas plays Miguel.

00:06:14.694 --> 00:06:18.010
And everyone was always
like, no one likes Miguel,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.740
Jon is the best sport about it all,

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.820
because everybody just
makes a joke about it.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.290
But yeah, it's a lot of fun.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:26.620
We just get to sort of see
each other, which is nice.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.290
It's like the phone
calls aren't quite enough

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:29.437
and the text chats.

00:06:29.437 --> 00:06:30.950
- No, getting to see each other

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.530
like any kind of zoom
or FaceTime or I agree.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.550
I mean, can you imagine what
this would be like without it,

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.717
without seeing people like
in a, just on a phone,

00:06:38.717 --> 00:06:41.720
you know, in the kitchen
with the Roseanne phone line,

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.000
that's like 10 feet long.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.653
Yeah, that would kill me.

00:06:46.489 --> 00:06:48.280
- Yeah. It wouldn't be
good, that's for sure.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.230
So grateful for technology.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:52.330
- Yeah. No, no, me too.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.340
So who of your, This Is
Us cast seem to be having

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:56.360
the best time in quarantine.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.740
Like when y'all talked, who's
like living their best life.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.399
- I think really me, honestly.

00:07:00.399 --> 00:07:01.887
(laughs)

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.670
I have to be honest, I
really like being at home.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:04.503
I really do.

00:07:04.503 --> 00:07:05.760
- You don't have kids right now,

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:08.120
so that's, there you go, that's why.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.670
You know what, I'm telling you that you're

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.763
having the best time.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.960
I don't know about
everybody else, but that's.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.362
I love, I love actually
getting to have the time,

00:07:16.362 --> 00:07:18.050
especially like, you know,

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.180
recently I've been waking up every morning

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.760
and coloring with them
and it's like a lot of,

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.920
kind of me time with
them and I've loved that.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.590
But at the same time, it's like,

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.650
Oh my gosh, I really want to
go to a dinner with adults

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.309
and just talk about adult thing.

00:07:28.309 --> 00:07:29.506
- Right, Right.

00:07:29.506 --> 00:07:32.130
I mean, I feel for
Sterling cause he and Ryan,

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.280
he and his wife, are, you know,

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:36.013
obviously teaching their
two sons and he's like,

00:07:36.013 --> 00:07:38.930
man, I got to run guys.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.230
I got, I gotta start a class.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.910
I gotta do this, we gotta do that.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:42.880
- Oh my gosh.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.910
- I know I don't, I don't listen.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.590
I can barely keep a succulent alive

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.100
that I started having in
the beginning of quarantine.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:52.620
- Succulents are like the
easiest plants to keep alive.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.114
- They don't need anything!

00:07:54.114 --> 00:07:55.330
- That's amazing,

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.470
that's why you're my
favorite human. Alright.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:07:59.830
Well there's something else that

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.630
I thought was kind of
cool that you're doing.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.670
So you have, it's a new
line at Walmart, right?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.694
A new clothing line.

00:08:05.694 --> 00:08:09.371
(overlapping chatter)

00:08:09.371 --> 00:08:10.750
You know that's a huge brand!

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.250
- I know, you know, it's funny.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.693
I was, when I was home,

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.760
I drove by the Walmart that my mom

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.990
and I had to like walk to
because my mom's car didn't work,

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.740
and it was super far.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:24.850
I mean it felt like 10 miles,

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.860
I think it was only four, but regardless

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.420
I was like, Oh my gosh,

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.530
I have this partnership
with a brand that I've been,

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.498
you know, literally shopping at forever,

00:08:32.498 --> 00:08:34.850
but when I was a young kid,

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:35.730
a chubby little girl,

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.480
like they didn't have cute clothes.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.220
There weren't cute girl clothes

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:42.890
for chubby girls or for anybody

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.610
that was sort of outside
of the straight size,

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:45.563
just generally.

00:08:46.904 --> 00:08:49.680
And now that they're
incorporating such incredible,

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.040
it's like affordable,
but it's also trendy.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:52.873
And I think that's really important

00:08:52.873 --> 00:08:54.640
cause I think when we feel good,

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.330
we do good and all of that,

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.960
it's all sort of encompassing.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.250
And so when I, you know,

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.340
was even approached by, by Walmart,

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:03.920
I was like, Oh, well, yeah.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.362
This makes sense for me
because it's something

00:09:05.362 --> 00:09:07.573
that I think is just.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:09.303
- I think it's real.

00:09:09.303 --> 00:09:10.540
That's what I like. It's believable.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:11.590
It's like I'm the same girl,

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:12.787
I shopped there too growing up.

00:09:12.787 --> 00:09:15.610
It's, I think, you know,

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:16.860
for some people they hear like,

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.240
Oh, well you don't need to be trendy.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.230
Like that's not important,

